Threats and mitigations
Compromised IoT device / spoofed telemetry: require hardware-backed device certificates, secure boot, signed firmware, and certificate revocation.

Man-in-the-middle interception: enforce TLS 1.3 and mutual TLS, pin trusted CA roots at gateways, and reject plaintext MQTT.

DDoS against dashboard ingestion: apply WAF/rate limits, autoscaling, MQTT quotas, and isolated message queues so the scheduler and Banker's-Algorithm engine from Part 1 is not directly exposed.

Cloud credential theft: use short-lived IAM roles, MFA for administrators, least privilege, and audit alerts for anomalous access.
